  "client_feedback": [
    {
      "date": "2026-10-26",
      "from": "Mark (EMBLEM-NLP), looking at design 2 on an iPhone",
      "said": "Not a fan of this composed hero image and the copy remains exactly the same as our first version which is an issue",
      "changes": [
        "The home hero is now a real photograph, not a composed image (a hand holding a phone; cropped, colour-matched and with a small printed maker's name retouched out) with the carrier logos on a white bar over its lower edge. The link preview image is a plain crop of the same photograph. No page may carry a composed image: imagery.max_composites_per_page is 0 and imagery.hero_not_composite is on.",
        "Design 2 has its own wording (designs/design-2/content.json and its own pages). distinctness.copy compares it with design 1 and fails a build that reuses design 1's page titles, descriptions, headings, sentences or phrases. Since the independent read of v4 and v5 found light rewrites that a strict match cannot see, a sentence counts as reused when it is 60% similar to one of design 1's (sentence_similarity 0.6, down from 0.85). The old build (v3) fails every one of those checks; the new one passes.",
        "New accuracy question: copy_written_for_this_design."
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-26",
      "from": "Mark (EMBLEM-NLP), looking at designs 1 and 2 on an iPhone",
      "said": "We don't like the mobile header menus on both versions",
      "changes": [
        "On phones design 3 keeps a slim header that stays in view: the engraved nameplate and one Menu button. The page links open in a sheet under the header, with a backdrop, a call button and a way out by Escape, by tapping outside or by choosing a link. Wide screens show the links as a row under a centred masthead. With scripts off, the links are listed under the nameplate (nojs.css)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-26",
      "from": "Mark (EMBLEM-NLP), asking for a third option",
      "said": "Give a 3rd complete redesign with royalty free images and imagery this 3rd option need to be luxurious",
      "changes": [
        "Design 3 (\"Lamplight\") is a complete third site: all 11 pages, its own layout, its own wording (designs/design-3/content.json and pages) and its own photography. A showroom after dark: garnet-black pages, champagne rules and type, Noto Serif Display with Jost, and carrier logos on pearl mount cards.",
        "Eleven royalty-free Pexels photographs (Pexels License, which allows commercial use without attribution; credits are on the Photo credits page anyway). None is a composite. People appear only as hands, with no faces. Printed maker names and labels were retouched out of four of them, and each retouch is listed on the credits page.",
        "Original imagery: the engine-turned patterns (a tile, a dial and a hallmark seal) are generated from a formula by designs/design-3/imagery/ornaments.py, so there is no licence to carry. The site's own favicon and touch icon are drawn the same way.",
        "distinctness.siblings lists designs 1 and 2: the wording, layout, palette and headline typeface must all differ from both."
      ]
    }
  ]
